rapidproto provides CMake targets and a code-generation helper:

    find_package(rapidproto CONFIG REQUIRED)

    # One call turns a schema into a linkable, header-only target (self-contained output).
    rapidproto_generate(my_schema
      PROTOS ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/schema.proto
      IMPORT_DIRS ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR})
    target_link_libraries(my_target PRIVATE my_schema)

rapidprotoc is a build-time (host) tool. When cross-compiling, depend on rapidproto with
"host": true in your vcpkg.json so the generator is built for the build machine.
